getOpaqueOrderInterval\(.*?^\}' $ordering=Extract $renderer '(?ms)^static CEntity \*\*OrderOpaqueBuildings\(.*?^\}' if($ordering -notmatch 'if\(!e \|\| !e->IsBuilding\(\)' -or $ordering -notmatch 'getOpaqueOrderInterval\(\s*\(rw::Atomic\*\)e->m_rwObject,entries\[i\]\.depth,true\)'){ throw 'Game layer must prove building type before passing static eligibility' } $registration=Extract $visibility '(?ms)#ifndef GTA_PS2?
 // This wrapper.*?#endif' if($registration -notmatch '\(rw::Atomic::RenderCB\)DefaultRenderCB_pushid' -or $registration -notmatch '#else\s+rw::vulkan::setOpaqueOrderDefaultRenderWrapper\(nil\)'){ throw 'Only audited non-PS2 default wrapper may be registered' } [IO.File]::WriteAllText((Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'opaque-order-wrapper.inc'),$wrapper) [IO.File]::WriteAllText((Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'opaque-order-classifier.inc'),$classifier) & (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'test-ragdoll.ps1') -KitRoot $KitRoot -OutDir $OutDir -Sources @('test-opaque-order-classifier.cpp') if($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0){throw 'Opaque order production classifier regression failed'}

#!/usr/bin/env python3 """Check patch bytes and apply the full series to the pinned LF upstream tree."""
import argparse from pathlib import Path import subprocess import tarfile import tempfile import unittest
BASE = "b050e1cc63b1869e6b514ab2f1a00ef4969e0c84" KIT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
def git(*args): return subprocess.run(["git", *map(str, args)], check=True, capture_output=True)
class PatchSeriesTests(unittest.TestCase): def test_patch_line_endings(self): patches = sorted((KIT / "patches").glob("*.patch")) self.assertTrue(patches) for patch in patches: with self.subTest(patch=patch.name): self.assertTrue(b"\r" not in patch.read_bytes(), "Patches must use LF")
def test_clean_lf_upstream(self): # Export only tracked source at the pinned revision; never copy local # game data, edits, or Git metadata. Override Windows autocrlf so this # exercises exactly the source bytes used by a clean Linux checkout. with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="lcvr-patches-") as directory: root = Path(directory) archive = root / "base.tar" git("-C", RE3, "-c", "core.autocrlf=false", "archive", "--format=tar", f"--output={archive}", BASE) source = root / "source" source.mkdir() with tarfile.open(archive) as tree: tree.extractall(source, filter="data") git("-C", source, "init", "-q") git("-C", source, "config", "core.autocrlf", "false") for patch in sorted((KIT / "patches").glob("*.patch")): try: git("-C", source, "apply", "--whitespace=nowarn", patch) except subprocess.CalledProcessError as error: # Stop here: later patches depend on earlier ones. self.fail(f"{patch.name}: {error.stderr.decode(errors='replace')}")
if __name__ == "__main__": parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__) parser.add_argument("re3", type=Path, help="Local clone containing the pinned re3 commit") args = parser.parse_args() RE3 = args.re3.resolve() unittest.main(argv=[__file__])

param(
    [Parameter(Mandatory=$true)][string]$StageRoot,
    [string]$OutDir = (Join-Path ([IO.Path]::GetTempPath()) ('lcvr-sleep-' + [Guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')))
)
$ErrorActionPreference='Stop'
function Extract([string]$s,[string]$pattern){
    $m=[regex]::Match($s,$pattern)
    if(-not $m.Success){throw "Missing production definition: $pattern"}
    $end=$m.Index+$m.Length;$depth=1
    while($depth -gt 0 -and $end -lt $s.Length){if($s[$end]-eq'{'){$depth++}elseif($s[$end]-eq'}'){$depth--};$end++}
    if($depth-ne0){throw 'Unterminated production block.'}
    $s.Substring($m.Index,$end-$m.Index)
}
$physical=[IO.File]::ReadAllText((Join-Path $StageRoot 'src/entities/Physical.cpp'))
$auto=[IO.File]::ReadAllText((Join-Path $StageRoot 'src/vehicles/Automobile.cpp'))
$clock=[IO.File]::ReadAllText((Join-Path $StageRoot 'src/core/QuestGameTime.h')).Replace('#include "Timer.h"','// Fixture timer adapter.')
$helperPath=Join-Path $StageRoot 'src/core/QuestPhysicsSleep.h'
if(-not(Test-Path $helperPath)){$helperPath=Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '../../overlay/src/core/QuestPhysicsSleep.h'}
$helper=[IO.File]::ReadAllText($helperPath).Replace('#include "QuestGameTime.h"','// Extracted gameplay clock above.').Replace('#include "World.h"','// Fixture world adapter.')
$functions=(Extract $physical '(?m)^void\s+CPhysical::ProcessControl\(void\)\s*\{')+"`n"+
    'bool CAutomobile::CheckSleep(){ bool skipPhysics=false;'+"`n"+
    (Extract $auto 'if\(!bIsStuck && \(GetStatus\(\) == STATUS_ABANDONED \|\| GetStatus\(\) == STATUS_WRECKED\)\)\s*\{')+"`nreturn skipPhysics; }`n"
[IO.File]::WriteAllText((Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'physics-sleep-timing-production.inc'),$clock+"`n"+$helper+"`n"+$functions,[Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false))
& (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'test-ragdoll.ps1') -KitRoot $StageRoot -OutDir $OutDir -Sources @('test-physics-sleep-timing.cpp')
if($LASTEXITCODE-ne0){throw 'Physics sleep timing regression failed.'}
# Every displacement producer/reset must update the reference-distance cache.
foreach($s in @($physical,$auto)){
    foreach($m in [regex]::Matches($s,'m_fDistanceTravelled = [^;]+;')){
        $tail=$s.Substring($m.Index+$m.Length)
        if($tail -notmatch '^\s*#if defined\(__ANDROID__\) && defined\(FIX_BUGS\)\s*m_fSleepDistance = QuestPhysicsSleep::ReferenceDistance\(m_fDistanceTravelled\);'){
            throw 'Displacement producer/reset is missing sleep-distance integration.'
        }
    }
}
$header=[IO.File]::ReadAllText((Join-Path $StageRoot 'src/entities/Physical.h'))
if($header-notmatch 'union \{ float m_phys_unused1; float m_fSleepDistance; \}') {throw 'Sleep cache must reuse existing storage.'}
Write-Host 'PASS: all displacement producers/resets update the sleep cache without changing object layout.'

param(
    [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][string]$ShaderTools,
    [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][string]$OutputDirectory
)
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
$root = [IO.Path]::GetFullPath((Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '../..'))
$output = [IO.Path]::GetFullPath($OutputDirectory)
if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $output) { throw 'Choose a new output directory.' }
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $output | Out-Null
$shader = Join-Path $root 'librw/src/vulkan/shaders/rw_postfx.frag'
$gain=[regex]::Match([IO.File]::ReadAllText($shader),'(?ms)^float ColourFilterGain\(.*?^\}')
if(-not $gain.Success){throw 'Production colour gain helper missing.'}
[IO.File]::WriteAllText((Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'postfx-colour-gain.inc'),$gain.Value)
foreach ($variant in @(@(0,1),@(1,0),@(1,1))) {
    $native=$variant[0];$integer=$variant[1]
    $binary = Join-Path $output "postfx-$native-$integer.spv"
    & (Join-Path $ShaderTools 'glslc.exe') --target-env=vulkan1.1 -O "-DRW_POSTFX_NATIVE=$native" "-DRW_POSTFX_INTEGER_STENCIL=$integer" -o $binary $shader
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'Postprocess shader compilation failed.' }
    & (Join-Path $ShaderTools 'spirv-val.exe') --target-env vulkan1.1 $binary
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'Postprocess shader validation failed.' }
    $assembly = (& (Join-Path $ShaderTools 'spirv-dis.exe') $binary) -join "`n"
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'Postprocess shader disassembly failed.' }
    if ($native -eq 1) {
        if ($assembly -match 'Binding [1-4]\b|OpImageGather|OpImageQuery') {
            throw 'Native postprocess retained temporal/upscale resources or operations.'
        }
        $samples = ([regex]::Matches($assembly, 'OpImageSample')).Count
        $fetches = ([regex]::Matches($assembly, 'OpImageFetch')).Count
        if ($integer -eq 1 -and ($samples -ne 4 -or $fetches -ne 5)) {
            throw "Native FXAA must use five integer stencil fetches and four filtered directional samples; found $fetches/$samples."
        }
        if ($integer -eq 0 -and ($samples -ne 9 -or $fetches -ne 0)) {
            throw 'Filtered native baseline must retain nine filtered reads and no integer fetches.'
        }
    } elseif ($assembly -notmatch 'Binding 4\b' -or $assembly -notmatch 'OpImageFetch') {
        throw 'General postprocess lost temporal/upscale support.'
    }
}
& (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'test-ragdoll.ps1') -OutDir (Join-Path $output 'host') -Sources @('test-postfx-native.cpp','test-postfx-colour.cpp','test-postfx-texels.cpp')
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'Postprocess policy tests failed.' }
Write-Host 'PASS: both postprocess shaders validate; native mode retains FXAA without temporal resources; fallback policy checked.'

#!/usr/bin/env python3 """Exercise privacy checks against disposable repositories with synthetic data."""
import importlib.util import os from pathlib import Path import shutil import subprocess import sys import tempfile import unittest
ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2] GUARD = ROOT / "tools/privacy_guard.py" DEVICE = b"2G" + b"X" * 12 HOST = b"fixture." + b"example.ts" + b".net" SPEC = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("privacy_guard", GUARD) MODULE = importlib.util.module_from_spec(SPEC) SPEC.loader.exec_module(MODULE)
class PrivacyGuardTests(unittest.TestCase): def setUp(self): cache = ROOT / ".cache" cache.mkdir(exist_ok=True) self.temp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="privacy-tests-", dir=cache) self.repo = Path(self.temp.name) self.env = os.environ.copy() # Isolate fixtures from the developer's Git configuration and identity. self.env["GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM"] = "1" self.env["GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL"] = os.devnull self.env["GIT_AUTHOR_NAME"] = self.env["GIT_COMMITTER_NAME"] = "Privacy Test" self.env["GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL"] = self.env["GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL"] = "test@example.invalid" self.run_git("init", "-q") self.run_git("config", "commit.gpgSign", "false") (self.repo / "safe.txt").write_text("safe\n") self.run_git("add", "safe.txt") self.run_git("commit", "-q", "-m", "Safe fixture")
def tearDown(self): def writable_remove(function, path, error): os.chmod(path, 0o700) function(path) shutil.rmtree(self.repo, onerror=writable_remove) self.temp.cleanup()
def command(self, args, data=None): return subprocess.run(args, input=data, cwd=self.repo, env=self.env, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)
def run_git(self, *args, data=None): result = self.command(["git", *args], data) self.assertEqual(result.returncode, 0, "Fixture Git operation failed") return result.stdout
def guard(self, *args, data=None): return self.command([sys.executable, str(GUARD), *args], data)
def blocked(self, result, private=DEVICE): self.assertNotEqual(result.returncode, 0) self.assertNotIn(private, result.stdout + result.stderr) self.assertNotIn(b"Traceback", result.stdout + result.stderr)
def push_input(self, oid=None, remote_ref="refs/heads/main"): oid = oid or self.run_git("rev-parse", "HEAD").decode().strip() return ("refs/heads/main " + oid + " " + remote_ref + " " + "0" * 40 + "\n").encode()
def install(self): (self.repo / "tools").mkdir() shutil.copy2(GUARD, self.repo / "tools/privacy_guard.py") shutil.copytree(ROOT / ".githooks", self.repo / ".githooks") for hook in (self.repo / ".githooks").iterdir(): hook.chmod(0o755) result = self.guard("install-hooks") self.assertEqual(result.returncode, 0)
def test_clean_tree_message_history_and_push(self): for mode in ("staged", "history"): self.assertEqual(self.guard(mode).returncode, 0) message = self.repo / "message.txt" message.write_text("Installed on personal Quest 3 device\n") self.assertEqual(self.guard("message", str(message)).returncode, 0) self.assertEqual(self.guard("pre-push", data=self.push_input()).returncode, 0)
def test_staged_blob_is_checked_even_if_working_file_was_cleaned(self): path = self.repo / "safe.txt" path.write_bytes(DEVICE) self.run_git("add", "safe.txt") path.write_text("clean working copy\n") self.blocked(self.guard("staged"))
def test_unstaged_data_is_not_part_of_commit(self): (self.repo / "safe.txt").write_bytes(DEVICE) self.assertEqual(self.guard("staged").returncode, 0)
def test_commit_message_is_blocked_without_echo(self): message = self.repo / "message.txt" message.write_bytes(b"Device " + DEVICE) self.blocked(self.guard("message", str(message)))
def test_deleted_historical_data_still_blocks_push(self): path = self.repo / "removed.bin" path.write_bytes(b"\x00" + DEVICE + b"\xff") self.run_git("add", "removed.bin") self.run_git("commit", "-q", "-m", "Synthetic binary fixture") self.run_git("rm", "removed.bin") self.run_git("commit", "-q", "-m", "Remove synthetic fixture") self.blocked(self.guard("history")) self.blocked(self.guard("pre-push", data=self.push_input()))
def test_old_commit_message_is_checked(self): message = self.repo / "message.txt" message.write_bytes(b"Synthetic " + DEVICE) self.run_git("commit", "-q", "--allow-empty", "-F", str(message)) self.blocked(self.guard("pre-push", data=self.push_input()))
def test_annotated_tag_message_is_checked(self): message = self.repo / "message.txt" message.write_bytes(b"Synthetic " + DEVICE) self.run_git("tag", "-a", "fixture", "-F", str(message)) oid = self.run_git("rev-parse", "refs/tags/fixture").decode().strip() self.blocked(self.guard("pre-push", data=self.push_input(oid, "refs/tags/fixture")))
def test_private_hostname_is_blocked(self): (self.repo / "safe.txt").write_bytes(HOST) self.run_git("add", "safe.txt") self.blocked(self.guard("staged"), HOST)
def test_private_filename_is_blocked_without_echo(self): name = DEVICE.decode() + ".txt" (self.repo / name).write_text("safe\n") self.run_git("add", name) self.blocked(self.guard("staged"))
def test_author_metadata_is_checked(self): self.env["GIT_AUTHOR_NAME"] = DEVICE.decode() self.run_git("commit", "-q", "--allow-empty", "-m", "Synthetic author fixture") self.blocked(self.guard("pre-push", data=self.push_input()))
def test_lowercase_device_value_is_blocked(self): (self.repo / "safe.txt").write_bytes(DEVICE.lower()) self.run_git("add", "safe.txt") self.blocked(self.guard("staged"), DEVICE.lower())
def test_old_filename_with_reused_clean_blob_is_checked(self): name = DEVICE.decode() + ".txt" shutil.copyfile(self.repo / "safe.txt", self.repo / name) self.run_git("add", name) self.run_git("commit", "-q", "-m", "Synthetic filename fixture") self.run_git("rm", name) self.run_git("commit", "-q", "-m", "Remove synthetic filename") self.blocked(self.guard("pre-push", data=self.push_input()))
def test_local_denylist_is_case_insensitive_and_not_echoed(self): value = b"synthetic-" + b"private-value" (self.repo / ".git/info/privacy-denylist").write_bytes(value + b"\n") (self.repo / "safe.txt").write_bytes(value.upper()) self.run_git("add", "safe.txt") self.blocked(self.guard("staged"), value.upper())
def test_private_checkpoint_namespace_is_blocked(self): self.blocked(self.guard("pre-push", data=self.push_input(remote_ref="refs/codex/fixture")))
def test_push_checks_only_outgoing_history(self): safe = self.run_git("rev-parse", "HEAD").decode().strip() message = self.repo / "message.txt" message.write_bytes(DEVICE) self.run_git("commit", "-q", "--allow-empty", "-F", str(message)) self.run_git("update-ref", "refs/codex/fixture", "HEAD") self.run_git("reset", "--hard", safe) self.assertEqual(self.guard("pre-push", data=self.push_input()).returncode, 0) self.blocked(self.guard("history"))
def test_ref_deletion_does_not_publish_history(self): line = "(delete) " + "0" * 40 + " refs/heads/old " + "a" * 40 + "\n" self.assertEqual(self.guard("pre-push", data=line.encode()).returncode, 0)
def test_malformed_input_and_git_failure_are_closed(self): self.blocked(self.guard("pre-push", data=b"invalid\n")) with self.assertRaises(MODULE.PrivacyError): MODULE.git("not-a-real-git-command")
def test_existing_custom_hook_path_is_preserved(self): self.run_git("config", "core.hooksPath", "custom-hooks") (self.repo / ".githooks").mkdir() for name in ("pre-commit", "commit-msg", "pre-push"): (self.repo / ".githooks" / name).write_text("#!/bin/sh\n") self.blocked(self.guard("install-hooks")) self.assertEqual(self.run_git("config", "core.hooksPath").strip(), b"custom-hooks")
def test_installed_git_hooks_block_real_commit_operations(self): self.install() (self.repo / "safe.txt").write_bytes(DEVICE) self.run_git("add", "safe.txt") self.blocked(self.command(["git", "commit", "-m", "Safe message"])) (self.repo / "safe.txt").write_text("safe update\n") self.run_git("add", "safe.txt") message = self.repo / "message.txt" message.write_bytes(DEVICE) self.blocked(self.command(["git", "commit", "-F", str(message)])) self.run_git("commit", "-q", "-m", "Safe update") self.assertEqual(self.guard("pre-push", data=self.push_input()).returncode, 0)
def test_installed_push_hook_blocks_historical_message(self): message = self.repo / "message.txt" message.write_bytes(DEVICE) self.run_git("commit", "-q", "--allow-empty", "-F", str(message)) self.install() remote = self.repo / "remote.git" self.run_git("init", "--bare", "-q", str(remote)) result = self.command(["git", "push", str(remote), "HEAD:refs/heads/main"]) self.blocked(result) refs = self.run_git("--git-dir=" + str(remote), "for-each-ref") self.assertEqual(refs, b"")
if __name__ == "__main__": unittest.main()

param(
    [string]$StageRoot = (Split-Path -Parent (Split-Path -Parent $PSScriptRoot)),
    [string]$OutDir = (Join-Path ([IO.Path]::GetTempPath()) ('vc-sprint-' + [Guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')))
)
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
$path = Join-Path $StageRoot 'src\peds\PlayerPed.cpp'
$source = [IO.File]::ReadAllText($path)
$parts = @(
    '(?ms)^static bool\r?\nIsRunWithoutLimitsCheatEnabled\(.*?(?=^#ifdef VC_PED_PORTS)',
    '(?ms)^static bool\r?\nUseQuestDirectionalLocomotion\(.*?(?=^void\r?\nCPlayerPed::SetRealMoveAnim)',
    '(?ms)^void\r?\nCPlayerPed::ProcessAnimGroups\(.*?^\}'
)
$definitions = @()
foreach ($pattern in $parts) {
    $match = [regex]::Match($source, $pattern)
    if (-not $match.Success) { throw "Cannot extract sprint production code: $pattern" }
    $definitions += $match.Value
}
if ($source -notmatch '(?ms)CPlayerPed::SetRealMoveAnim\(void\)\s*\{\s*if\(BlendQuestLocomotionToIdle\(this\)\)') {
    throw 'VR stop blend is not wired into SetRealMoveAnim.'
}
$pedSource = [IO.File]::ReadAllText((Join-Path $StageRoot 'src\peds\Ped.cpp'))
if ($pedSource -notmatch 'if\(ApplyQuestMovementVelocity\(this\)\)') {
    throw 'VR directional velocity is not wired into CalculateNewVelocity.'
}
foreach ($pattern in @('(?ms)^static bool\r?\nApplyQuestMovementVelocity\(.*?^\}', '(?ms)^float\r?\nCPed::WorkOutHeadingForMovingFirstPerson\(.*?^\}')) {
    $match = [regex]::Match($pedSource, $pattern)
    if (-not $match.Success) { throw "Cannot extract directional movement production code: $pattern" }
    $definitions += $match.Value
}
[IO.File]::WriteAllText((Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'quest-sprint-production.inc'), ($definitions -join "`n"), [Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false))
$general = [IO.File]::ReadAllText((Join-Path $StageRoot 'src/core/General.h'))
$angle = [regex]::Match($general, '(?ms)^\tstatic float GetRadianAngleBetweenPoints\(.*?^\t\}')
if (-not $angle.Success) { throw 'Cannot extract engine heading convention.' }
[IO.File]::WriteAllText((Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'quest-sprint-angle.inc'), $angle.Value)
$animHeader = [IO.File]::ReadAllText((Join-Path $StageRoot 'src\animation\AnimManager.h'))
$enum = [regex]::Match($animHeader, '(?ms)^enum AssocGroupId.*?^\};')
if (-not $enum.Success) { throw 'Cannot extract actual animation group enum.' }
$animSource = [IO.File]::ReadAllText((Join-Path $StageRoot 'src\animation\AnimManager.cpp'))
$arrays = [regex]::Matches($animSource, '(?ms)^char const\s*\*\s*aPlayer(?:WithRocket|1Armed|2Armed|BBBat|StrafeBack|StrafeLeft|StrafeRight)?Animations\[\] = \{.*?^\};')
if ($arrays.Count -ne 8) { throw 'Cannot extract eight forward/strafe/back movement animation mappings.' }
[IO.File]::WriteAllText((Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'quest-sprint-anims.inc'), $enum.Value + "`n" + (($arrays | ForEach-Object { $_.Value }) -join "`n"), [Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false))
Copy-Item -LiteralPath (Join-Path $StageRoot 'src\weapons\WeaponType.h') -Destination (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'quest-sprint-weapon-types.inc')
Write-Host ('PlayerPed.cpp SHA256: ' + (Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $path -Algorithm SHA256).Hash)
& (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'test-ragdoll.ps1') -KitRoot $StageRoot -OutDir $OutDir -Sources @('test-quest-sprint.cpp')

#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Verify the production radio/driving/firing boundary without game assets."""
from pathlib import Path
import re
import subprocess
import tempfile
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
driving=(root/'overlay/src/vr/QuestDrivingVR.cpp').read_text()
weapons=(root/'overlay/src/vr/QuestWeaponVR.cpp').read_text()
def method(text,name):
    match=re.search(r'(?ms)^(?:static )?(?:void|uint32)\s+'+name+r'\(.*?^}',text)
    assert match,name
    return match.group()
code='\n'.join(method(driving,n) for n in ['MapButtonDriveBy','UpdateQuestDrivingInput','ApplyQuestVehicleButtonInput'])
code+='\n'+method(weapons,'UpdateWeaponTriggerEdges')
call=re.search(r'(?s)if\(inVehicle\)\s*UpdateWeaponTriggerEdges\([^;]+;',weapons).group()
code+='\nvoid ProductionFireEdgeGate(bool menu,bool gameplay,uint32 vehicleCapturedHands,bool inVehicle,const androidgame::PadInput &input){'+call+'}\n'
with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix='radio-driving-') as d:
    work=Path(d);(work/'production.inc').write_text(code)
    (work/'main.cpp').write_text(r'''
#include <cassert>
#include <cstdio>
#include <cstdint>
#include <algorithm>
#define nil nullptr
using uint32=uint32_t;using int16=int16_t;
constexpr int VR_HAND_COUNT=2;
template<class T,class U,class V>T clamp(T v,U a,V b){return std::max(T(a),std::min(v,T(b)));}
struct CControllerState {int Square=0,Cross=0,Circle=0,LeftShoulder1=0,RightShoulder1=0,LeftShoulder2=0,RightShoulder2=0;void Clear(){*this={};}};
struct CVehicle {void*pDriver=nullptr;bool IsRealHeli(){return false;}bool IsRealPlane(){return false;}bool IsCar(){return true;}bool IsBike(){return false;}} vehicle;
int player;CVehicle*FindPlayerVehicle(){return &vehicle;}void*FindPlayerPed(){return &player;}
struct CPad {int GetMode(){return 0;}static CPad*GetPad(int){static CPad pad;return &pad;}};
namespace androidgame {struct PadInput{bool x=false,b=false,a=false;float leftTrigger=0,rightTrigger=0,leftGrip=0,rightGrip=0;}input;const PadInput&GetPadInput(){return input;}}
namespace QuestRadio {bool active=false;bool Update(bool blocked){if(blocked)active=false;return false;}bool Interacting(){return active;}void SuppressDriving(CControllerState*s){if(active)s->Clear();}}
namespace OculusVR {
CVehicle*gButtonDriveByVehicle=nullptr;int gButtonDriveByDirection=-1;
bool gVehicleForwardFireEnabled=true,gVrRadioChangeJustPressed=false;
bool physical=false;uint32 bikeBlocked=0,carBlocked=0;bool motionBlocked=false;
bool gPoseValid[2]={true,true},gTriggerPressed[2]={},gTriggerJustPressed[2]={},gTriggerJustReleased[2]={};
float gTrigger[2]={};int gHeldSlot[2]={-1,-1};
constexpr int VR_DRIVING_DEFAULT=0;int GetDrivingTypeForVehicle(CVehicle*){return physical?1:0;}
void LoadDrivingSettings(){}bool IsVrDrivingActive(){return physical;}bool IsImmersiveDrivingActive(){return physical;}bool IsTrackedWeaponHeld(int h){return gHeldSlot[h]>=0;}
bool IsQuestVehicleThirdPerson(){return false;}bool IsVrCarActive(){return physical;}bool IsVrBikeActive(){return false;}bool IsQuestDrivingHandUnavailable(int){return false;}
uint32 UpdateImmersiveBikeInput(const float*,const androidgame::PadInput&,uint32 blocked){bikeBlocked=blocked;return 0;}
uint32 UpdateImmersiveCarInput(const float*,uint32 blocked){carBlocked=blocked;return 0;}
void UpdateMotionInput(const androidgame::PadInput&,bool blocked){motionBlocked=blocked;}
void MapHornToPad(CControllerState*){}void MapHandbrakeToPad(CControllerState*s,bool on){if(on)s->LeftShoulder1=255;}
#include "production.inc"
}
int main(){
 using namespace OculusVR;vehicle.pDriver=&player;auto &input=androidgame::input;CControllerState state;
 input.rightTrigger=.8f;input.leftTrigger=.6f;input.b=true;
 assert(UpdateQuestDrivingInput(&state,false)==0);ApplyQuestVehicleButtonInput(&state,false);
 assert(state.Cross>0 && state.Square>0 && gButtonDriveByVehicle==&vehicle);
 QuestRadio::active=true;assert(UpdateQuestDrivingInput(&state,false)==3);
 assert(bikeBlocked==3 && carBlocked==3 && motionBlocked);
 ApplyQuestVehicleButtonInput(&state,false);
 assert(state.Cross==0 && state.Square==0 && state.Circle==0 && gButtonDriveByVehicle==nullptr);
 physical=true;gHeldSlot[1]=2;
 ProductionFireEdgeGate(false,true,3,true,input);assert(!gTriggerPressed[1] && !gTriggerJustPressed[1]);
 QuestRadio::active=false;UpdateQuestDrivingInput(&state,false);ApplyQuestVehicleButtonInput(&state,false);
 ProductionFireEdgeGate(false,true,3,true,input);assert(gTriggerPressed[1] && gTriggerJustPressed[1]);
 assert(state.Cross>0 && !motionBlocked);
 ProductionFireEdgeGate(true,true,0,true,input);assert(!gTriggerPressed[1]);
 puts("Production driving integration: radio captures throttle/brake, wheel/motion input and both native/physical firing; ordinary input restores correctly.");
}
''')
    exe=work/'test';subprocess.run(['c++','-std=c++17',str(work/'main.cpp'),'-o',str(exe)],check=True)
